                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "optema":</h3><p><b>Optema</b> was a brand name for a series of microphone capsules manufactured by CAD in its Conneaut factory in Ohio beginning in the late 1990s.</p><p><a href="/images/mic_extras/cad/OS110.jpg" rel="shadowbox"><img src="/images/mic_extras/cad/OS110-sm.jpg" width="200" alt="CAD Optema OS-110 capsule" /></a><br />The <b>OS 110</b> capsule had a 33mm outside diameter. It used 28mm diaphragms made of 3-micron &#8220;high-strength polymer film.&#8221; This was a center-terminated capsule, described in company literature at the time as a &#8220;vintage capsule design.&#8221; The backplate drilling pattern appears to have been inspired by the <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/tag/k67">Neumann K-67</a>.</p><p>Here is a <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/mistamindiy/5537535837/">photo of an OS-110 capsule</a> in an E-350.</p>
